/P 214 0 R
/E (    You cannot see something's shape when you are in the middle of it. You're too near. The perceiving is being done by your emotions. However, something shifts when you take a step back and describe it as if you were an outsider. When you were living it, you were blind to the patterns. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5 6]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 214 0 R
/E (    The practice of prosoche, or "mindful attention," is directly related to stoic philosophy. The Stoics understood that seeing clearly is impeded by emotional entanglement. However, distance \(even imagined distance\) brings clarity back. )
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
